Feature: SQL Transformation Logic Update for pat_account Table

  The SQL logic for the pat_account table must be updated to align with the latest source-to-target mapping specifications. This includes transformation rules for prescriber_id, patient_sf_id, hash_key, and last_modified_date. The update must ensure data quality, consistency, and accurate downstream reporting.

  Background:
    Given the source table purgo_playground.p_account contains columns:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_name_c | prescriber_name_c_address | patinet_c | recordtypeid | id | accountid |
    And the target table purgo_playground.pat_account contains columns:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_id | prescriber_key | patient_sf_id | service_request_type | case_sf_id | account_id | hash_key | last_modified_date |
    And the mapping specification is provided in source_target_mapping_specifications.xlsx
    And the SQL script is maintained in pat_account_sql_script.sql

  # Happy Path Scenarios

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_id with uppercase and conditional 'DR.' prefix
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = "john smith"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_id in the target should be "DR.JOHN SMITH"

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_id when 'Dr.' prefix is already present (case-insensitive)
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = "Dr. Alice"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_id in the target should be "DR.ALICE"

  Scenario Outline: Transform prescriber_id for various input cases
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = <input>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_id in the target should be <expected>
    Examples:
      | input         | expected      |
      | "john smith"  | "DR.JOHN SMITH" |
      | "Dr. Alice"   | "DR.ALICE"      |
      | "DR. Bob"     | "DR.BOB"        |
      | "dr. Carol"   | "DR.CAROL"      |
      | "DR. DAN"     | "DR.DAN"        |

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_key with conditional 'DR.' prefix from prescriber_name_c_address
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = "michael brown"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_key in the target should be "DR.MICHAEL BROWN"

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_key when 'Dr.' prefix is already present (case-insensitive)
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = "Dr. Susan"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_key in the target should be "DR.SUSAN"

  Scenario Outline: Transform prescriber_key for various input cases
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = <input>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_key in the target should be <expected>
    Examples:
      | input           | expected         |
      | "michael brown" | "DR.MICHAEL BROWN" |
      | "Dr. Susan"     | "DR.SUSAN"         |
      | "DR. Lee"       | "DR.LEE"           |
      | "dr. Kim"       | "DR.KIM"           |
      | "DR. TOM"       | "DR.TOM"           |

  Scenario: Transform patient_sf_id only if patinet_c contains 'PAT'
    Given a source record with patinet_c = "PAT12345"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then patient_sf_id in the target should be "PAT12345"

  Scenario: Set patient_sf_id to NULL if patinet_c does not contain 'PAT'
    Given a source record with patinet_c = "ABC12345"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then patient_sf_id in the target should be NULL

  Scenario Outline: Transform patient_sf_id for various patinet_c values
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <input>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then patient_sf_id in the target should be <expected>
    Examples:
      | input      | expected    |
      | "PAT001"   | "PAT001"    |
      | "PAT002"   | "PAT002"    |
      | "123PAT"   | "123PAT"    |
      | "XYZ123"   | NULL        |
      | "PAT"      | "PAT"       |
      | "pat123"   | NULL        |

  Scenario: Transform hash_key by concatenating patinet_c, recordtypeid, and id with underscore delimiter
    Given a source record with patinet_c = "PAT001", recordtypeid = "SR01", id = "CASE123"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then hash_key in the target should be "PAT001_SR01_CASE123"

  Scenario Outline: Transform hash_key for various input values
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <patinet_c>, recordtypeid = <recordtypeid>, id = <id>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then hash_key in the target should be <expected>
    Examples:
      | patinet_c | recordtypeid | id      | expected             |
      | "PAT001"  | "SR01"       | "CASE1" | "PAT001_SR01_CASE1"  |
      | "PAT002"  | "SR02"       | "CASE2" | "PAT002_SR02_CASE2"  |
      | "123PAT"  | "SR03"       | "CASE3" | "123PAT_SR03_CASE3"  |
      | "XYZ123"  | "SR04"       | "CASE4" | "XYZ123_SR04_CASE4"  |

  Scenario: Populate last_modified_date with current ETL execution timestamp
    Given a source record is processed
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then last_modified_date in the target should be set to the current timestamp in ISO 8601 format

  # Error Scenarios

  Scenario: Error when prescriber_name_c is NULL
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = NULL
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col     | error_message                       |
      | prescriber_id | "prescriber_name_c is NULL"         |

  Scenario: Error when prescriber_name_c_address is NULL
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = NULL
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col      | error_message                          |
      | prescriber_key | "prescriber_name_c_address is NULL"    |

  Scenario: Error when patinet_c is NULL
    Given a source record with patinet_c = NULL
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col     | error_message                |
      | patient_sf_id | "patinet_c is NULL"          |

  Scenario: Error when recordtypeid is NULL for hash_key
    Given a source record with recordtypeid = NULL
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col | error_message                |
      | hash_key  | "recordtypeid is NULL"       |

  Scenario: Error when id is NULL for hash_key
    Given a source record with id = NULL
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col | error_message            |
      | hash_key  | "id is NULL"            |

  Scenario: Error when all hash_key components are NULL
    Given a source record with patinet_c = NULL, recordtypeid = NULL, id = NULL
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col | error_message                    |
      | hash_key  | "All hash_key components are NULL" |

  # Validation Rules

  Scenario Outline: Validate prescriber_id transformation
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = <input>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_id must be uppercase and prefixed with "DR."
    Examples:
      | input         |
      | "john smith"  |
      | "Dr. Alice"   |
      | "DR. Bob"     |
      | "dr. Carol"   |

  Scenario Outline: Validate prescriber_key transformation
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = <input>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_key must be uppercase and prefixed with "DR."
    Examples:
      | input           |
      | "michael brown" |
      | "Dr. Susan"     |
      | "DR. Lee"       |
      | "dr. Kim"       |

  Scenario Outline: Validate patient_sf_id transformation
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <input>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then patient_sf_id must be set to <expected>
    Examples:
      | input      | expected    |
      | "PAT001"   | "PAT001"    |
      | "XYZ123"   | NULL        |

  Scenario Outline: Validate hash_key transformation
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <patinet_c>, recordtypeid = <recordtypeid>, id = <id>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then hash_key must be <expected>
    Examples:
      | patinet_c | recordtypeid | id      | expected             |
      | "PAT001"  | "SR01"       | "CASE1" | "PAT001_SR01_CASE1"  |
      | "XYZ123"  | "SR04"       | "CASE4" | "XYZ123_SR04_CASE4"  |

  Scenario: Validate last_modified_date format
    Given a source record is processed
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then last_modified_date must be a valid timestamp in ISO 8601 format

  # Data-driven ETL Logging

  Scenario Outline: ETL log entry for each processed record
    Given a source record with patient_sf_id = <patient_sf_id>, prescriber_id = <prescriber_id>, hash_key = <hash_key>, account_id = <account_id>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an ETL log entry should be created in pat_account_etl_log with
      | patient_sf_id | prescriber_id | hash_key | account_id | last_modified_date | error_message |
      | <patient_sf_id> | <prescriber_id> | <hash_key> | <account_id> | <last_modified_date> | NULL |
    Examples:
      | patient_sf_id | prescriber_id   | hash_key             | account_id | last_modified_date      |
      | "PAT001"      | "DR.JOHN SMITH" | "PAT001_SR01_CASE1"  | "ACC001"   | "2024-06-01T12:00:00Z"  |
      | "PAT002"      | "DR.ALICE"      | "PAT002_SR02_CASE2"  | "ACC002"   | "2024-06-01T12:01:00Z"  |

  # WHERE Clause Validation

  Scenario: Validate WHERE clause filter for patinet_c LIKE '%PAT%'
    Given the transformation logic is applied
    When the WHERE clause is evaluated
    Then only records where patinet_c contains 'PAT' (case-sensitive) are processed

  Scenario: Error if WHERE clause excludes valid patient_sf_id
    Given a source record with patinet_c = "pat123"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then the record should not be processed and no entry should be created in pat_account

  # Schema Validation

  Scenario: Validate last_modified_date column exists in pat_account table
    Given the pat_account table schema
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then last_modified_date column must exist and be of type timestamp

  Scenario: Error if last_modified_date column is missing in pat_account table
    Given the pat_account table schema does not include last_modified_date
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with
      | error_col         | error_message                        |
      | last_modified_date| "last_modified_date column missing"  |
